serve-tui-tools-without-http-sessions

Lane: bugfix

FlatPatch: serve-tui-tools-without-http-sessions

Form: GitDiff

Segment: none

Purpose: Keep TUI dynamic tools reachable through daemon MCP connections across TUI listener replacement.

Requires: none

Provides: Serve sessionless MCP discovery, rebind session-injected TUI endpoints on reattachment, and inherit live parent endpoints when starting or reloading children while retaining tool policy.

Boundary: Preserve active threads, session-static settings, configured MCP servers, other connected clients, and native authentication, managed requirements and approval enforcement.

Verification: The TUI daemon lifecycle scenario covers legacy sessionless discovery and listener replacement; core configuration and child-start tests cover retained policies, reloads, managed rejection and stale captured endpoints.


